        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-347",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "jose/jwe.py:_decrypt_and_auth decrypts BEFORE authenticating on the AES-CBC-HMAC path: `plaintext = encryption_key.decrypt(...)` runs at line 246 while the auth-tag comparison is deferred to line 247. The underlying CBC decrypt (CryptographyAESKey.decrypt) performs PKCS7 unpadding with no try/except, so `unpadder.finalize()` raises an uncaught ValueError on bad padding and escapes before the MAC is ever checked \u2014 a padding oracle distinguishable from the JWEError('Invalid JWE Auth Tag') returned on MAC failure. The encrypt-then-MAC protection is present but applied too late to be effective. Note the GCM branch DOES wrap decryption and re-raise JWEError (line 506), making the CBC branch the inconsistent one.\n\nVerifier (CONFIRM): Re-derived from source. jose/jwe.py:_decrypt_and_auth does decrypt-then-MAC on the AES-CBC-HMAC path: auth_tag_check is computed at line 239 but the comparison/reject is at lines 247-248, AFTER the CBC decrypt+PKCS7 unpad at line 246. A PKCS7 failure in CryptographyAESKey.decrypt (cryptography_backend.py:512-514) therefore unwinds out of _decrypt_and_auth before line 247 is ever evaluated, so the attacker gets JWEError(\"Invalid padding bytes.\") for bad padding vs JWEError(\"Invalid JWE Auth Tag\") for a MAC mismatch -- an observable discrepancy that is a classic Vaudenay CBC padding oracle enabling plaintext recovery without the MAC key. The encrypt-then-MAC construction is present but gated too late to prevent it, exactly as the lead says, and the file's own comment at jwe.py:182-183 quotes the RFC 7516 requirement it violates. I CORRECT one analyst detail: the claim of \"no try/except\" in the CBC path is FALSE -- cryptography_backend.py:495 opens a try whose line 517-518 \"except Exception as e: raise JWEError(e)\" catches the ValueError. The oracle survives anyway because the distinguishing information is the error MESSAGE, not an uncaught exception type. Reachability verified in source and graph: jwe.decrypt (public API, jwe.py:60) -> _decrypt_and_auth (jwe.py:185) -> CryptographyAESKey.decrypt; lines 237-248 are reachable_from_entry=true, hop_distance=1; A128CBC-HS256/A192CBC-HS384/A256CBC-HS512 are in ALGORITHMS.HMAC_AUTH_TAG (constants.py:67) and ALGORITHMS.SUPPORTED (constants.py:70), map to modes.CBC (cryptography_backend.py:428-430), and CryptographyAESKey is the active AESKey (backends/__init__.py:22-23), so the flawed branch is live on a default install. Also noted independently: line 247 compares tags with \"!=\" instead of hmac.compare_digest (non-constant-time, CWE-208). Severity MEDIUM rather than HIGH because both failures raise the same exception CLASS, so exploitation depends on the embedding application surfacing/distinguishing the exception text; in any app that logs or returns str(e) this rises to HIGH. Applicable CWEs: CWE-347 (integrity tag verified too late), with CWE-696 (incorrect behavior order) and CWE-209/CWE-203 (observable discrepancy / padding oracle) as the precise manifestation. Exploit-reference check was attempted and returned \"exploit corpus unavailable: not indexed\", so no published-module or patched-version evidence was established either way; this verdict rests purely on source I read."
